title: Pam_Dumpster
---
<<set_left CharacterManager Pamella>>
<<wait .15>>
<<set_right CharacterManager Francine>>
<<wait .15>>
<<left CharacterManager>>
<<wait .15>>
Pamella: Hey, Francine?
Pam’s smiling, which is somehow worse than if she were glaring at you. Not by much, but still.
Pamella: Was it you I saw in the dumpster behind the theatre yesterday?
The smile looks much more like a predator baring her teeth, now. You were, in fact, in the dumpster behind the theatre yesterday – but that’s where you get your stuff! You have a family to disguise!
-> No, that was someone else.
    Pamella: Really?
    <<right CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Francine: Yeah, haha, I saw that too – it was like… a possum– or a raccoon, or something!
    <<left CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Pamella: Mhm.
    <<right CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Francine: …yeah, there’s a big pest problem here. I mean, have you noticed how many rats are around campus?
    <<left CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Pamella: No, I guess I missed that. I must have missed the giant, human-sized rats. And the fact that there’s one that looks exactly like you. Wearing an identical trench coat. That must have just slipped past me.
    <<right CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Francine: …haha…someone should…really do something about that.
    <<left CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Pamella: Yeaaaah, someone should.
    You soothe how awkward you feel at the following silence with the reassurance that at least you won’t be known as the dumpster girl.
-> …yes?
    Pamella: Oh my GOD I knew it!
    Cine races to hold up your arms as Pam puts her hands on your shoulders.
    Pamella: and I agree with you completely.
    …what?
    <<right CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Francine: What?
    <<left CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Pamella: They always toss those costumes as soon as they think the production’s over –
    <<right CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Francine: – and sometimes even when there’s only one hole in them –
    <<left CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Pamella: –YES– and there’s always leftover fabric. It’s TRAGIC.
    <<right CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Francine: Yes! You should come next time!
    The conversation stops, both of you surprised at what you just said.
    Francine: Um.. or not, just–
    <<left CharacterManager>>
    <<wait .15>>
    Pamella: Fine, I’ll come. But you’d better save some of the good stuff. I’m good enough to work with scraps, but I don’t deserve them.
<<ending CharacterManager>>
===
